0.012.0	Wed Oct 14 09:10:15 PM EDT 2026
    [ New Features ]
    - GET /pivot: crosstab/pivot table.  Accepts ?rows=, ?cols=, and
      ?m=col:fn:alias (sum|avg|min|max|count|count_distinct); ?totals=1
      adds subtotals and a grand-total row; ?h= applies post-aggregation
      HAVING filters; ?topn=N+?topn_col= keeps the top-N row groups;
      ?max_cols=N collapses tail column combos into "Other";
      ?format=csv|sqlite|json|xlsx exports the result.
    - GET /stats: per-column statistics (row count, null count, distinct
      count, min, max, mean, median).
    - GET /scatter: scatter/bubble plot (?x=, ?y=, ?series=, ?size=,
      ?scheme=, ?min_r=, ?max_r=).  The scatter panel now exposes all
      parameters: "Colour by" (any column), "Bubble size" (numeric
      columns only), colour scheme (tableau10|category10|set2|set3|paired
      -- enabled only when a series column is chosen), and Min/Max radius
      1-40 (enabled only when a size column is chosen).  ?scheme= is
      validated server-side; an unrecognised name returns 400.
    - GET /stacked: stacked bar chart (?cat=, ?series=, ?val=).
    - GET /combo: combo bar+line chart (?cat=, ?bar_val=, ?line_val=).
    - GET /treemap: treemap (?group=, ?size=, ?topn=N).
    - GET /histogram: histogram with server-side binning (?col=, ?bins=N;
      default 10 bins; max 200).
    - GET /line: alias for GET /graph (all /graph params accepted).
    - GET /graph: new ?series=<col> parameter for multi-series line charts.
    - Calculated fields (Database::BI::Calc): recursive-descent evaluator
      supporting arithmetic, comparison, IF, string, numeric, and date
      functions; bin(); coalesce; isnull.  All chart and pivot routes
      accept ?c=name:expr (repeatable).  Stored fields managed via
      GET /calc/list, POST /calc/save, POST /calc/delete.
    - Date normalisation: stored date-format patterns convert non-ISO
      columns to ISO-8601 before aggregation.  Managed via
      GET /dates/list, POST /dates/save, POST /dates/delete.
    - Named value groups: virtual "${col}_group" columns map raw values
      to analyst-defined labels.  Managed via GET /groups/list,
      POST /groups/save, POST /groups/delete.
    - Redis backend: DataSource accepts redis => 'redis://...' and the
      redis:tablename|redis://... spec format.

    [ Enhancements ]
    - GET /join and GET /combine now support pagination (?page=N,
      ?per_page=M, ?sort=<col>, ?dir=asc|desc).
    - GET /export and POST /export now accept ?page=N and ?per_page=M.
    - f= filters and d=1 dedup applied before pagination so the N+1
      row count reflects the reduced set (reduce-before-paginate).
    - bar_view and pie_view: new ?topn=N parameter; remainder collapsed
      into "Other".
    - Added X-BI-Warnings response header to GET /export.
    - All chart render() calls now use a unified chart_html stash key
      and include a chart => { kind, title, encode, options } DTO.
    - Added DataSource::dbi_source() for SQL-capability detection and
      Database::Join zero-copy ATTACH path.
    - Added _grouped_totals() as the single aggregation entry point for
      all chart routes, with SQL push-down and Perl fold fallback.

    [ Bug Fixes ]
    - /join and /combine: no-params default now returns the first 200
      rows with a pagination bar, consistent with /view and /open.
    - f= filters on paginated views no longer produce short pages.
    - d=1 dedup now deduplicates the full result before slicing.
    - has_next recomputed after in-memory filter/dedup reduction.
    - Chart category order no longer changes when a filter is applied:
      Perl fold now returns groups in the same ascending key order as
      the SQL path.
    - Aggregation on SQLite sources pushes SQL-compatible f= filters to
      the database; non-SQL-able filters still fall back to Perl fold.
    - DataSource::dbi_source() no longer propagates exceptions from
      non-SQL backends; returns undef instead.
    - CSV and other non-SQL sources no longer emit "Bad limit clause"
      warnings; LIMIT/OFFSET is only sent to SQL-backed sources.

    [ Dependencies ]
    - HTML::D3 >= 0.20 (radius_range support for scatter bubble charts;
      0.19 added the five new snippet methods).
    - Database::Abstraction >= 0.51 (redis key support).
    - Database::Join >= 0.009.0 (aggregate, limit/offset, dbi_source).

0.011.0	Sun Oct 11 09:20:48 PM EDT 2026
    [ Enhancements ]
    - Added schema browser (GET /tables) for multi-table SQLite databases.
      Opening a SQLite file with more than one internal table now shows a
      card grid listing every table with its columns rather than silently
      opening the first table.  Clicking a card opens that table via the
      existing /open view.  The schema page is inserted into the breadcrumb
      trail so users can navigate back to it.
    - Added ?it=<table> parameter to GET /open, allowing a specific internal
      table to be opened from a multi-table SQLite file.
    - Added sqlite_tables() accessor to DataSource, returning the list of
      internal table names discovered during construction.
    - Added internal_table constructor option to DataSource, letting callers
      request a specific internal SQLite table instead of the auto-detected
      first match.
    - Added data/store.db: sample SQLite database with three joinable tables
      (customer, product, sales) for development and demonstration.
    - Fixed: multi-table symlink for .db-extension SQLite files now uses
      .sql as the symlink extension so Database::Abstraction opens it via
      the DBI/SQLite backend rather than falling through to the CSV reader.
    NOTE: /tables tests currently cover SQLite only.  MySQL, PostgreSQL,
    and other multi-table driver tests will be added in a future release
    once the corresponding Database::Abstraction drivers are available.
    - Server-side pagination for /view/:table and /open.  Both routes now accept
      ?page=N (1-based, default 1) and ?per_page=M (default 200, max 2000).
      The controller uses the N+1 trick: it requests per_page+1 rows via
      LIMIT/OFFSET and treats the extra row as a "has next page" sentinel rather
      than issuing a COUNT(*) query.  This is critical for multi-GB SQLite files
      (e.g. openaddresses.db) where COUNT(*) would block the server for minutes.
      A pagination bar (Prev / current page / Next) is shown when at least two
      pages exist.  All URL parameters (filters, dedup, per_page, etc.) are
      preserved across page navigations.
    - BerkeleyDB files larger than 100 MB now return an informative error page
      instead of causing disk thrashing.  Files whose magic bytes identify them as
      BerkeleyDB but whose DB_File tie() fails (e.g. Berkeley DB version 9 files
      opened with libdb-5.3) would previously fall through to D::A's CSV path,
      causing a full read of the binary file.  DataSource now detects the magic
      bytes in _detect_file_info, refuses files above 100 MB immediately, and
      returns error_unsupported_db for smaller files where tie() fails.
    - Three-level breadcrumb for chart pages.  When a bar, line-graph, pie,
      or heatmap chart is launched from a table view that was itself reached
      from the schema browser (/tables), the chart page now shows the full
      navigation chain (e.g. Home > Store schema > Table view > Chart) rather
      than the previous two-level "Home > Back to table".  The dashboard
      panel forms forward the current page's back_url as back2=/back2_label=
      parameters; the chart controllers promote them to the outer breadcrumb
      level so all four levels are rendered correctly.
    - SQLite hover tooltip on the home-page file picker.  Hovering over a
      database card in the "Choose a database" list now shows a dark popover
      with the file type (e.g. "SQLite database - 3 tables"), last-modified
      date, and file size.  GET /api/stat now returns a table_count integer
      for SQLite-extension files (.sql, .sqlite, .sqlite3, .db); the count
      is omitted for Berkeley DB .db files or other non-SQLite payloads.
      The home-page db-cards now carry data-path attributes so the JS fetch
      can call /api/stat on first mouseenter (lazy, not on page load).

0.010.0	Tue Oct  6 11:29:33 AM EDT 2026
    [ Enhancements ]
    - Added Folder view (GET /folder): browse any data file grouped by the
      letter prefix of a chosen code column (e.g. Order # values like A10,
      CT4, B3).  Records are organised into a two- or three-level folder
      hierarchy -- top level shows distinct first letters (A-Z), clicking a
      letter reveals sub-prefix folders (e.g. CA, CB, CC inside C) and any
      items with that exact prefix, clicking a sub-prefix shows the matching
      records in a table.  A "Folder view..." toolbar button opens a column-
      picker panel identical in style to the chart panels; the code column is
      auto-detected when the panel is opened but the user can override it via
      the dropdown.  Breadcrumb navigation lets the user step back to any
      folder level or return to the source table via "Back to table".
    - upload_file now guards move_to() with eval { ...; 1 } and checks -f
      $dest after the call.  A failed save returns a JSON 500 with the key
      error_upload_save instead of propagating an unhandled exception.
      The orphaned upload subdirectory is removed before the error response
      is sent.  (Uses the eval { ...; 1 } idiom to avoid false positives
      from a stale $@ left by Mojolicious internal dispatch code.)

    - All chart pages (/graph, /pie, /heatmap, /bar) now use responsive SVG
      layout (HTML::D3 0.18 `responsive => 1`): charts scale to the available
      container width so they render correctly on mobile and narrow windows.
    - /bar: added ?max=N parameter -- when N > 0, bars beyond the top N are
      collapsed into a single "Other" bar (HTML::D3 `max_bars`).  Prevents
      unreadable charts from high-cardinality categorical columns.
    - /bar: category-column name is now shown as an axis label below the bars
      (HTML::D3 `x_label`).
    - /pie: added ?scheme= parameter to select the D3 categorical colour
      palette (tableau10, category10, set2, set3, paired; default tableau10).
      Mirrors the existing ?scheme= parameter already on /heatmap.
    - /join: added ?jtype=left|inner|outer parameter to control join semantics.
      `left` (default) keeps all rows from the left table; `inner` returns
      only rows that match in both; `outer` returns all rows from either table.
      Exposed in the "Merge data" panel as a "Which rows to include" dropdown.
    - /join: schema-type-mismatch warnings from Database::Join (e.g. "column
      'score' has type TEXT in left table but INTEGER in right table") are now
      captured and displayed as a yellow notice bar above the data table,
      instead of landing silently in the server error log.
    - DataSource now implements updated() -- proxies to Database::Abstraction's
      updated() or stats the file directly.  This allows Database::Join to
      invalidate its SQLite spill cache when a source file changes on disk.

